 "landed_note": "S81-SERDES 10-19: lp.py landed column from the wires-only flat parent ot_pdie_serdes_col_flat (spec tools/landed_parent/specs/ot_pdie_serdes_col.json). Clock families (COORDINATOR LEAD-S81 10-19 11:53): clk -> ck_tx, ck_ptx; pma_rck (recovered, NOT the core PLL) -> ck_syn, ck_dly, ck_chn, ck_out. The only rck->clk crossings are the CDC children u_rm (closed gray-FIFO rate matcher, elastic IDLE deletion) and u_sts (2-flop status syncs) plus the regional reset runs (>= 4 stages per region = synchronisers); no landing crosses the families. related_same_frequency is the landed-cluster STA convention (as the closed s81lk_rate_match tile); the CDC is structural, proven by tb_s81_pdie_col with die B 300 ppm slow.",
